 Yeah, yeah.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:15.360
 Michael Faraday?

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:15.880
 Oh, great.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:18.120
 He was incredibly popular, because it was the early days

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.160
 when he was doing it.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.480
 Yeah, 19 series of lectures.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:23.400
 And his most famous one, I think he delivered it several years,

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.120
 maybe, was called the Chemical History of a Candle.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.320
 And it's one of those wonderful things,

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.520
 because it sounds wonderful.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.200
 It's one of the most successful science books ever.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:34.440
 And his basic point was, so much of what we know about science

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:36.800
 can be encapsulated in a candle, whether that's

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.360
 what the Wig is made of, what the sort of what the air around it

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.920
 does, the sort of flow of air when it's burning.

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:44.080
 The science of combustion, all of these things

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.040
 come together in the form of a candle.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.840
 It was written as a book which I think

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:52.160
 might be still in print today, nearly 200 years later on.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:55.200
 And he was dead against writing it as a book,

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.160
 because he said the point about science

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.840
 to communicate it to people is it has to be

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:00.040
 in a live environment.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.960
 Lectures are an important way of properly communicating

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:04.400
 science to people.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.880
 And then, in the 1850s, there was a massive wave of sayances,

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.320
 which swept across London.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:13.240
 And he thought, OK, maybe not enough people know any science.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:15.920
 And so he thought, OK, I will do it as a book now,

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.160
 because it can get the word out a bit more.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.480
 And I got the book out of the library today.

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:21.480
 Did you?

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:22.480
 Yeah, yeah.

